.TH WATCHER\-CAPTURE 1 "2026" "The Watcher" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
watcher\-capture \- record a shell session for The Watcher's graded debrief
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B watcher\-capture
.B \-\-attach
.RB [ \-\-platform
.IR platform ]
.RB [ \-\-target
.IR box ]
.RB [ \-\-web ]
.br
.B watcher\-capture
.B \-\-export
.I file
.RB [ \-\-platform
.IR platform ]
.RB [ \-\-target
.IR box ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B watcher\-capture
records the commands you run against a target \(em every command, its output and
the gaps between them \(em by driving your shell through a userspace PTY (openpty on
Unix, ConPTY on Windows).
It uses
.B no eBPF, ptrace or kernel hooks
and needs no root.
The capture is turned into a graded debrief by The Watcher: a per\-phase audit across
MITRE ATT&CK, the Unified Kill Chain and CWE.
.PP
In
.B \-\-attach
mode the session streams into the running Watcher app live.
In
.B \-\-export
mode it is written to a session file you can later drop into the app \(em useful on a
cloud box such as HTB Pwnbox, where the file is pulled back over SSH.
Processing is deterministic and happens on your machine; nothing is uploaded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-attach
Stream the session into the running Watcher app as you work. Type
.B exit
to stop capturing.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " file"
Write the session to
.I file
instead of streaming. Hack as normal; type
.B exit
to finish, then import the file into the app.
.TP
.BI \-\-platform " platform"
The training platform:
.BR htb ", " thm ", " offsec ", " immersive " or " local .
.TP
.BI \-\-target " box"
The box or target name, recorded with the session.
.TP
.B \-\-web
Also fold HTTP attacks from Burp Suite (via its MCP Server) onto the same timeline.
Off by default; in\-scope traffic only, with auth headers, cookies and tokens stripped
before anything is stored. See
.B docs/web\-capture.md
in the project.
.TP
.BI \-\-machine " name"
Override the recorded machine/host label.
.TP
.BI \-\-context " path"
Set the working\-context path recorded with the session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Capture a Hack The Box run live:
.PP
.RS
.EX
watcher\-capture \-\-attach \-\-platform htb \-\-target blurry
.EE
.RE
.PP
Capture to a file inside Pwnbox for later import:
.PP
.RS
.EX
watcher\-capture \-\-export ~/.watcher\-exports/run.json \-\-platform htb \-\-target blurry
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.watcher\-exports/
Default location suggested for exported session files.
